    /* ── About ── */
    'about.hero.tag':         'ABOUT',
    'about.hero.title':       '<em>About</em>',
    'about.hero.subtitle':    'A human approach to personal finance',
    'about.intro':            '<strong>Welcome.</strong>',
    'about.p1':               'This blog was born from a deep curiosity about finance — not just its mathematical or technical aspects.',
    'about.p2':               'Yes, I love understanding numbers, investments, retirement, compound interest, and how money grows over time. But what interests me even more is everything surrounding money and the way it shapes our daily lives.',
    'about.p3':               'Why do some people earn good salaries yet live in constant stress? Why is it so hard to talk about money with our children, our partner, or our family? Why do some financial decisions bring a sense of freedom while others create anxiety, guilt, or pressure?',
    'about.p4':               'Finance goes beyond financial products and investments. It touches marriage, relationships, family wealth, gifts, the cost of living, rent increases, our relationship with work, our ambitions, and even our personal definition of success.',
    'about.p5':               'It\'s this more human, psychological, and realistic vision of money that I wanted to explore through this blog.',
    'about.p6':               'I read a great deal on finance, economics, the psychology of money, human behavior, and wealth management. Many of these books draw on research, statistics, studies, and concrete data. I love taking these concepts, understanding them deeply, then thinking about how they can realistically apply to our reality here in Québec.',
    'about.p7':               'I share book summaries, reflections, and commentary on various books that push you to think differently about money, work, time, and success.',
    'about.p8':               'I also take various courses and training in different finance-related areas, including taxation, family wealth, and other topics that directly affect our financial lives. I\'m someone who constantly seeks to learn, to better understand, and to keep growing.',
    'about.p9':               'This blog is a space where I share what I learn, what I observe, and how these concepts can be applied concretely in our everyday lives.',
    'about.p10':              'I don\'t claim to have all the answers, nor to replace professional advice tailored to your personal situation. I simply love to learn, analyze, and make financial topics more accessible from a human angle.',
    'about.p11':              'This blog aims to be different from what you typically find in Québec. We talk as much about financial psychology as investment, as much about human behavior as about numbers.',
    'about.sunday':           '<strong>New articles are published every Sunday.</strong>',
    'about.newsletter':       'For those who want to receive new publications, book summaries, and stay informed about new articles, feel free to sign up for the newsletter to receive an email whenever new content is published.',
    'about.closing':          'I sincerely hope this blog will inspire you to think differently about money and to have more open conversations about a topic that has an enormous influence on all of our lives.',
    /* ── My Story ── */
    'histoire.hero.breadcrumb':       'My Story',
    'histoire.hero.title':            'I don\'t have all<br><em>the answers.</em>',
    'histoire.lead':                  '"This blog doesn\'t exist to give lessons. It exists to connect with people who, like me, have an unconventional path and a deep desire to do better financially."',
    'histoire.p1':                    'I\'m not a financial planner or an investment expert. I\'m simply a curious woman, passionate about personal finance, who decided to share her journey, her thoughts, and her trial and errors.',
    'histoire.p2':                    'I didn\'t come from a wealthy family. I was a single mom at a very young age. I had no <em>handout</em>, no magic shortcut, no big head start in life. For a long time, I truly believed money was for other people. For me, having $20,000 in savings would already have been something huge.',
    'histoire.p3':                    '<strong>And yet.</strong>',
    'histoire.h2.debut':              'How I Started',
    'histoire.p4':                    'At a certain point in my life, I was working as a consultant while taking on a few small contracts on the side under my own name. Honestly, I had no grand plan. I simply wanted to make ends meet.',
    'histoire.p5':                    'I built my own website with very little resources. I learned SEO, online marketing, social media. And gradually, clients started coming.',
    'histoire.p6':                    'Then one day, I realized something that completely changed my perspective: <strong>the income from my small contracts was exceeding my main salary.</strong>',
    'histoire.pullquote':             '"I was living below my means. And that\'s how, gradually, I managed to save $100,000 since the pandemic."',
    'histoire.h2.montant':            'What That Amount Changed',
    'histoire.p7':                    'That amount completely transformed the way I see money. Not just from a financial standpoint, but mentally too. I understood that money wasn\'t something to fear or reserved for an elite.',
    'histoire.p8':                    'So I started listening to podcasts, reading finance books, and joining an investment book club. <strong>TFSA, RRSP, ETFs, compound interest</strong> — words no one had ever explained to me in school.',
    'histoire.h2.ecole':              'What School Never Taught Me',
    'histoire.p9':                    'Today, what fascinates me isn\'t just saving. It\'s understanding how to build real financial freedom. I deeply believe it\'s possible for ordinary people to become more financially solid, even without an extraordinary income.',
    'histoire.p10':                   'I also believe strongly in the power of small amounts invested with discipline. Whether through self-employment, extra income, or a few hundred dollars a month in passive income — everything becomes powerful when you invest consistently over many years.',
    'histoire.h2.recommencer':        'Don\'t Be Afraid to Start Over',
    'histoire.p11':                   'I know what it\'s like to go to school with a child to care for, to work, to be exhausted. I know what it feels like to think you\'re behind everyone else.',
    'histoire.p12':                   'But sometimes, <strong>accepting temporary hardship to build something more solid completely changes a life.</strong>',
    'histoire.p13':                   'This blog is my financial lab. I\'ll be sharing my ideas, my reflections, my successes, my mistakes, and my financial adventures.',
    'histoire.p14':                   'And if some of you see yourselves in this… <strong>Welcome to my madness.</strong>',
    'histoire.sidebar.title':         'Open Your TFSA',
    'histoire.sidebar.body':          'It\'s what I use. Free, simple, no hidden fees.',
