    'dwz.h2.start':           'If you start with $50 every 2 weeks',
    'dwz.p13':                'You think $50 every 2 weeks isn\'t enough to change your life? Let the numbers speak.',
    'dwz.p14':                '<strong>$50 × 26 times/year = $1,300/year invested.</strong> Total over 20 years: <strong>$26,000 out of your pocket.</strong>',
    'dwz.proj.low.label':     'Conservative scenario',
    'dwz.proj.mid.label':     'Realistic scenario',
    'dwz.proj.high.label':    'Optimistic scenario',
    'dwz.proj.invested':      'Invested: $26,000',
    'dwz.highlight':          'You invest <strong>$26,000</strong> out of your pocket over 20 years — and you come out with between <strong>$59,000 and $118,000</strong> depending on returns. That\'s the magic of compound interest: your money generates interest, that interest generates interest, and it snowballs exponentially over time.',
    'dwz.h3.means':           'What that means concretely',
    'dwz.p15':                'At 14%/yr — the historical NASDAQ return over 20 years — your biweekly $50 becomes <strong>4.5x your investment</strong>. You put in $26,000. You get back $118,000.',
    'dwz.p16':                'And if you put that in your <strong>TFSA</strong>? Zero tax on those $92,000 in gains. 100% in your pocket.',
    'dwz.h2.conclusion':      'My conclusion — Die With Zero applied',
    'dwz.p17':                'This book didn\'t tell me to stop investing. It told me to invest <em>intelligently</em> — and to live <em>now</em>.',
    'dwz.p18':                'Today my strategy is simple:',
    'dwz.p19':                '&nbsp;<strong>$7,000/year in my TFSA</strong> → automatic, stress-free<br><strong>My capital works on its own</strong> → compound interest does the rest<br><strong>The rest of my income?</strong> → live, travel, enjoy',
    'dwz.p20':                'I don\'t need to stress. My million is on its way. And in the meantime, I\'m living my life.',
    'dwz.p21':                'That\'s real financial freedom.',
    'dwz.disclaimer':         '⚠️ Note: I am not a financial planner. This article shares my personal experience — not official financial advice. Consult a professional for your specific situation.',
